1
00:00:00,825 --> 00:00:02,204
Last time, we asked:

2
00:00:02,224 --> 00:00:04,934
A magnet, a steel pin and a copper wire!

3
00:00:05,204 --> 00:00:07,474
The pin and the wire are both metal.

4
00:00:07,764 --> 00:00:09,444
Which one will the magnet pull?

5
00:00:09,499 --> 00:00:10,899
One, the steel pin.

6
00:00:12,149 --> 00:00:13,689
Two, the copper wire.

7
00:00:14,949 --> 00:00:15,969
Three, both.

8
00:00:17,455 --> 00:00:18,965
Hold on to your answer!

9
00:00:21,437 --> 00:00:25,317
Today, a brand-new theme begins, and it starts with magnets!

10
00:00:25,824 --> 00:00:28,274
A little pigeon is hiding in this video.

11
00:00:28,524 --> 00:00:29,764
Can you spot it?

12
00:00:29,889 --> 00:00:31,589
Pigeons love our void deck.

13
00:00:31,649 --> 00:00:33,949
Look up high, on the ledges and the pipes!

14
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,460
You against the Buddies!

15
00:00:35,730 --> 00:00:37,580
Lock in first with your fingers.

16
00:00:37,850 --> 00:00:39,680
One finger for every point.

17
00:00:40,261 --> 00:00:41,591
Today you'll learn:

18
00:00:41,791 --> 00:00:43,281
What a magnet is.

19
00:00:43,483 --> 00:00:44,953
What attract means.

20
00:00:45,155 --> 00:00:46,815
Magnetic materials.

21
00:00:47,317 --> 00:00:48,257
Are you ready?

22
00:00:48,697 --> 00:00:49,467
Three!

23
00:00:49,847 --> 00:00:50,507
Two!

24
00:00:50,877 --> 00:00:51,527
One!

25
00:00:51,947 --> 00:00:52,667
Go!

26
00:00:54,056 --> 00:00:54,946
Round one!

27
00:00:55,246 --> 00:00:56,906
Which one will the magnet pull?

28
00:00:57,206 --> 00:00:58,506
Show me your fingers!

29
00:01:01,981 --> 00:01:02,961
Locked in!

30
00:01:03,089 --> 00:01:03,819
One!

31
00:01:03,959 --> 00:01:07,609
In Grandma's sewing box, a magnet picks up the steel pins.

32
00:01:07,669 --> 00:01:08,949
I have seen it!

33
00:01:08,999 --> 00:01:09,809
Two.

34
00:01:10,009 --> 00:01:13,169
The copper wire is thinner and lighter, so it should be easier

35
00:01:13,189 --> 00:01:14,029
to pull.

36
00:01:14,079 --> 00:01:15,079
Three, both!

37
00:01:15,099 --> 00:01:17,769
They are both metal, and my magnet pulls metal.

38
00:01:17,989 --> 00:01:18,839
Easy!

39
00:01:19,115 --> 00:01:22,365
Basil, your magnet is smooth and painted, like a toy.

40
00:01:22,535 --> 00:01:24,185
Is it made of plastic?

41
00:01:24,831 --> 00:01:25,961
Look closer.

42
00:01:26,571 --> 00:01:30,211
Long ago, people found a special kind of rock that pulls on

43
00:01:30,231 --> 00:01:30,901
iron.

44
00:01:30,921 --> 00:01:34,181
A natural magnet is also called a lodestone.

45
00:01:34,702 --> 00:01:37,682
A lodestone is a magnet that comes from the ground.

46
00:01:37,872 --> 00:01:39,292
Nobody made it!

47
00:01:39,312 --> 00:01:42,122
Now look inside Basil's magnet.

48
00:01:42,702 --> 00:01:46,922
Under the paint, it is made of metal, usually iron or steel.

49
00:01:47,445 --> 00:01:51,545
And magnets come in lots of shapes: bar, U-shaped, button, rod, ring

50
00:01:51,565 --> 00:01:52,615
and horseshoe!

51
00:01:55,316 --> 00:01:56,476
Say it with me!

52
00:01:57,182 --> 00:02:00,282
A magnet is an object that is usually made of iron or

53
00:02:00,302 --> 00:02:01,152
steel.

54
00:02:03,781 --> 00:02:04,971
Be a steel pin!

55
00:02:05,251 --> 00:02:06,241
Shrink down.

56
00:02:06,511 --> 00:02:07,451
Quietly.

57
00:02:09,734 --> 00:02:12,644
You are a steel pin, lying on the test table.

58
00:02:13,384 --> 00:02:17,004
Beside you, the copper wire looks like a big orange pipe.

59
00:02:17,517 --> 00:02:21,347
Here comes the magnet, like a giant red and blue tower.

60
00:02:22,117 --> 00:02:24,967
It is still far away, so nothing happens.

61
00:02:25,486 --> 00:02:27,066
Closer, and closer.

62
00:02:27,856 --> 00:02:29,066
You feel a tug.

63
00:02:29,856 --> 00:02:30,856
Then whoosh!

64
00:02:31,626 --> 00:02:34,936
You slide across the gap, and click onto the magnet.

65
00:02:35,457 --> 00:02:37,027
The magnet lifts you up.

66
00:02:37,837 --> 00:02:38,837
Look down.

67
00:02:39,607 --> 00:02:42,927
The copper wire and the eraser have not moved at all.

68
00:02:44,586 --> 00:02:46,776
The answer is one: the steel pin!

69
00:02:47,036 --> 00:02:48,576
Did you show one finger?

70
00:02:48,846 --> 00:02:50,208
Put one finger up!

71
00:02:50,228 --> 00:02:52,788
The magnet pulled the steel pin across the gap.

72
00:02:52,858 --> 00:02:55,191
But the copper wire did not move at all!

73
00:02:55,211 --> 00:02:58,711
Pip, the copper wire is very light, but the magnet still did

74
00:02:58,731 --> 00:02:59,691
not pull it.

75
00:02:59,961 --> 00:03:02,161
So being light is not the reason.

76
00:03:02,299 --> 00:03:03,299
My turn!

77
00:03:03,429 --> 00:03:05,339
I tested Mum's iron wok.

78
00:03:05,389 --> 00:03:08,549
The magnet could not lift it, so the wok is not attracted

79
00:03:08,569 --> 00:03:09,639
to the magnet!

80
00:03:09,769 --> 00:03:11,329
Something is not right.

81
00:03:11,599 --> 00:03:13,779
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

82
00:03:14,059 --> 00:03:15,019
Hold on!

83
00:03:20,432 --> 00:03:21,562
Arms crossed?

84
00:03:21,832 --> 00:03:23,042
One finger up!

85
00:03:23,094 --> 00:03:23,964
Watch.

86
00:03:24,224 --> 00:03:26,974
When I let go, the magnet holds on to the side of

87
00:03:26,994 --> 00:03:27,614
the wok.

88
00:03:27,954 --> 00:03:29,564
The wok is attracted.

89
00:03:29,794 --> 00:03:31,794
It is just too heavy to lift!

90
00:03:31,921 --> 00:03:35,571
A fridge magnet cannot lift your fridge either, but it holds on

91
00:03:35,591 --> 00:03:36,721
to the fridge door.

92
00:03:36,844 --> 00:03:39,174
So my magnet sticks to the wok, like glue!

93
00:03:39,374 --> 00:03:40,924
Is my magnet sticky?

94
00:03:41,575 --> 00:03:43,695
Look closer, in slow motion.

95
00:03:44,275 --> 00:03:47,585
The pin starts to move before it touches the magnet.

96
00:03:48,145 --> 00:03:49,819
It jumps across the gap.

97
00:03:49,839 --> 00:03:52,059
The magnet pulls the pin towards it.

98
00:03:52,629 --> 00:03:55,179
We say the magnet attracts the pin.

99
00:03:55,969 --> 00:03:57,159
Attract means pull!

100
00:03:57,299 --> 00:04:00,079
My magnet pulls the pin, even before they touch.

101
00:04:00,209 --> 00:04:01,765
So it is not sticky at all!

102
00:04:01,785 --> 00:04:04,625
The pin is made of steel, and the nail is made of

103
00:04:04,645 --> 00:04:05,445
iron.

104
00:04:06,025 --> 00:04:08,735
They are made of magnetic materials.

105
00:04:09,252 --> 00:04:13,022
Magnetic materials are the materials that a magnet attracts.

106
00:04:13,242 --> 00:04:15,942
Iron and steel are magnetic materials!

107
00:04:18,645 --> 00:04:19,945
Say it with me!

108
00:04:20,654 --> 00:04:23,954
Magnets attract objects made of magnetic materials.

109
00:04:24,454 --> 00:04:27,194
Magnetic materials include iron and steel.

110
00:04:29,674 --> 00:04:31,134
Show me your score hand!

111
00:04:31,414 --> 00:04:32,804
One finger or more?

112
00:04:33,124 --> 00:04:34,484
You beat the Buddies.

113
00:04:34,754 --> 00:04:35,784
Two fingers?

114
00:04:36,064 --> 00:04:37,074
High five!

115
00:04:37,646 --> 00:04:39,096
Did you spot the pigeon?

116
00:04:39,376 --> 00:04:41,506
It was on top of the bicycle rack!

117
00:04:41,635 --> 00:04:43,115
Here is a fun fact!

118
00:04:43,195 --> 00:04:46,625
Scientists think pigeons can sense the Earth's magnetism.

119
00:04:46,695 --> 00:04:50,275
It helps them find their way home, even from far away!

120
00:04:50,402 --> 00:04:51,682
Tell someone at home!

121
00:04:52,411 --> 00:04:54,611
Let's read today's key words together!

122
00:04:54,901 --> 00:04:55,661
Ready?

123
00:04:55,948 --> 00:04:56,808
Magnet.

124
00:04:58,159 --> 00:04:58,959
Attract.

125
00:05:00,407 --> 00:05:01,907
Magnetic materials.

126
00:05:03,892 --> 00:05:04,832
Well done!

127
00:05:05,629 --> 00:05:06,329
Wait!

128
00:05:06,409 --> 00:05:08,899
Copper is a metal, just like iron and steel.

129
00:05:09,109 --> 00:05:11,743
So why does my magnet ignore the copper wire?

130
00:05:11,763 --> 00:05:13,353
Find out in Part Two!

131
00:05:14,513 --> 00:05:15,614
Say it with us!

132
00:05:16,414 --> 00:05:17,164
Ready?

133
00:05:17,288 --> 00:05:17,948
One!

134
00:05:18,288 --> 00:05:18,988
two!

135
00:05:19,293 --> 00:05:20,468
Now you know!
